  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The initial charge on the capacitor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>V</mi></math>. If after closing the&nbsp; switch the charge flown through the circuit is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>, the charge on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></math>. The potential across the capacitors will be same. Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>V</mi></math></p>",
